<h2>How We Arrived At These Rates to Find the Best Fort Myers Home Insurance.</h2>
<p>The first variable in determining your optimal Fort Myers home insurance rate is the calculation of your <strong>Dwelling Coverage</strong> amount. Dwelling Coverage refers to the part of your homeowner’s policy that covers the <strong>physical structure of your home</strong>; in other words, it would cover the cost of rebuilding or repairing your house in the case of damage caused by covered perils.</p>
<p><strong>To calculate your Dwelling Coverage</strong>, you need to <strong>estimate the cost to rebuild your home</strong>. This isn’t the same as the market price of your home, but rather the cost of materials and labor to rebuild it from scratch.</p>
<p>Typically, local construction costs and the square footage of your home are key indicators used to calculate this figure. It’s essential to ensure your Dwelling Coverage amount is accurate, as underinsuring could leave you with out-of-pocket costs, while over insuring means you’re spending more on premiums than necessary.</p>
<h3>How to Find Your Home Insurance Dwelling Coverage Amount</h3>
<p>Your <strong>heated area</strong> is the amount of space in your house that is air conditioned (usually excluding the garage, lanai, etc.) and is <strong>generally the main variable used to estimate the amount for Dwelling Coverage</strong> on your homeowners insurance policy.</p>
<p>For Fort Myers, the cost to rebuild a house is about <strong>$175 per square foot of heated area</strong>. The <strong>most common heated area for a house in Fort Myers is about 1800 square feet.</strong> </p>
<p>In this example, that would mean that we would expect the <strong>most common Dwelling Coverage amount in Fort Myers to be about $315,000</strong>. Keep in mind that you can insure the house for more or less than this amount, but if you mortgage your home, your mortgage lender will probably require a certain amount of Dwelling Coverage to satisfy the loan. </p>
<p>For houses in Fort Myers, our agents use the <a href="https://leepa.org">Lee County Property Appraiser’s website (leepa.org)</a> to find the heated area of your Fort Myers home.</p>
<p>Also, the house <strong>building years that we chose reflect the peak home building years for Fort Myers</strong>, so there’s a good chance that your house was built during or close to one of these peak years. Fort Myers also has a lot of older houses that were built between 1910 and 1970, but we didn’t include those in this table because they vary wildly with how they’ve changed and been remodeled over time.</p>
